ing", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "6fe18981-d508-4fa7-9e51-f4410d87a3f3", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284290.693309, "updated_at": 1790284290.693309, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "sibling_fields_used": ["content"], "sibling_field_chars": {"content": 30}, "text": "Worked for a couple of seconds", "text_chars": 30, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "920778d1-d559-41ea-b448-e70a72bbdff7", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284290.696472, "updated_at": 1790284292.608496, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "bio", "content_type": "code", "part_kinds": [], "sibling_fields_used": ["text"], "sibling_field_chars": {"text": 399}, "text": "Use this conversation as the user's dedicated fantasy-football workspace for two leagues: Sleeper is an established dynasty league the user has played in for roughly 3–4 years; Yahoo Fantasy is a brand-new redraft league. The user plans to ingest rosters/lineups and work through lineup decisions, roster construction, waivers, trades, dynasty value, and weekly strategy separately for each league.\n", "text_chars": 399, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f06fe596-459d-4a4b-bd8f-52ae42d36792", "role": "tool", "role_name": "bio", "created_at": 1790284294.231695, "updated_at": 1790284294.231695, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "assistant", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "Model set context updated.", "text_chars": 26, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8e958884-708b-481a-805c-e30e2ad6591f", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284294.917654, "updated_at": 1790284305.473901, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "Perfect. We’ll treat this as the **control room for both fantasy football leagues**, but keep the two completely separated so dynasty logic never bleeds into redraft logic.\n\n- **Sleeper — Dynasty:** established roster, 3–4 years of history. We’ll care about current production **plus** age curves, contracts/role stability, draft capital, future picks, trade windows, rebuild vs. contention, taxi/IR, and multi-year roster value.\n- **Yahoo — Redraft:** brand-new team. We’ll optimize much more aggressively for **this season**: weekly starts/sits, waivers, streaming, injuries, matchups, playoff schedule, roster churn, and points now.\n\nWhen you ingest each lineup, I want to capture the **league settings too**—scoring, roster slots, number of teams, Superflex/1QB, TE premium, PPR format, keeper rules if any, waiver system, and for Sleeper your future picks. Those settings can radically change player value.\n\nThen I can maintain a running view for each team: **starters → bench → IR/taxi → positional strengths/holes → expendable assets → waiver targets → trade targets → weekly decisions**.\n\nSend me whichever roster you want first. Screenshots are fine; we can reconstruct the whole thing from them.", "text_chars": 1205, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds